[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":40},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-7,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25,"_26":27},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":38,"_13":38,"_29":39},"id","basico-flor","nome","The daisy","rascunho",false,"html","<p>The daisy is the easiest way to start the white <a href=\"/en/glossary#cruz\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The 4 edges of one face (usually white) in place, lined up with the centers. The first step of the beginner method and of CFOP.\">cross</a>: you gather the 4 white edges around the <strong>yellow</strong> center, with white facing up. It looks like a yellow flower with white petals. There is no algorithm here: just a few turns, and you will understand each one.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F2 R2 B2 L2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/d38cb3a170d3c03e.svg\" alt=\"The finished daisy, seen from above.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The finished daisy, seen from above.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>The diagrams in this step show only the centers and the white edges. The rest of the cube doesn&#39;t matter now.</p>\n<h2>Before each turn: make room</h2>\n<p>Each petal takes one of the 4 places around the yellow center. Before bringing an edge up, turn the top (<code>U</code>) until the place it will take has <strong>no white</strong>. That way you don&#39;t knock off a petal that was already done.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R2 U&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;U F2&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"U F2\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/5c28840c4ec65409-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/5c28840c4ec65409-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/5c28840c4ec65409-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>There is already a petal in front and the edge is below it: <code>U</code> moves the petal out of the way, and only then <code>F2</code> brings the edge up.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>The white edges, one at a time</h2>\n<p>Look for a white edge and see where it is.</p>\n<p><strong>On the bottom, with white facing down.</strong> Turn the face it is on twice. It comes up with white facing up.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F2&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"F2\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/ebb7ae624f2cde1e-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/ebb7ae624f2cde1e-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>The white is on the bottom, in front (you can&#39;t see it). <code>F2</code> brings the edge up.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p><strong>In the middle.</strong> Turn the face on the side of the white in the direction that takes the edge up. The white arrives facing up.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;R&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"R\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/12a7017b00d4d19a-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/12a7017b00d4d19a-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>The white is in front; the edge is on the right face, which goes up with <code>R</code>.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F'&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"F'\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/c04cef04dfa89fa8-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/c04cef04dfa89fa8-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>The white is on the right; the edge is on the front face, which goes up with <code>F&#39;</code>.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p><strong>On top, with white on the side.</strong> The edge is in place, but flipped. Turn the front face once (<code>F</code>): it goes down to the middle and you are in the previous case.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F R&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"F R\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/400e1ed8b4ba06cb-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/400e1ed8b4ba06cb-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/400e1ed8b4ba06cb-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>White facing the front: <code>F</code> takes the edge down to the middle, and <code>R</code> brings it up with white on top.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p><strong>On the bottom, with white on the side.</strong> Turn the face it is on (<code>F</code>, for example): it goes to the middle, and again it is the middle case.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;L' F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F L'&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"F L'\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/e19b2e9c9dd3adc3-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/e19b2e9c9dd3adc3-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>L'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/e19b2e9c9dd3adc3-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>White facing the front, on the bottom: <code>F</code> takes the edge to the middle, and <code>L&#39;</code> brings it up with white on top.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>Repeat until all 4 petals are on top.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> don&#39;t think about the order of the petals or their other colors. That is for the next step.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","treino","metodos",[33],"anterior",{"_13":31,"_29":32},"proximo",{"_13":28,"_29":30},"grupos",[],"White cross","endereco","/3x3/basico/cruz","Before you start","/3x3/basico/antes",{"_13":34,"_35":36,"_29":37},"Beginner method","numero",2,"/3x3/basico#flor","3x3","/3x3/",{"_41":42,"_43":44},"cubos",[47,48,49,50,51,52,53],"idiomas",[45,46],"pt","en",{"_11":38,"_13":38},{"_11":62,"_13":62},{"_11":61,"_13":61},{"_11":60,"_13":60},{"_11":58,"_13":59},{"_11":56,"_13":57},{"_11":54,"_13":55},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","2x2"]
